  'zcc-r71-interchange-contractor-appointed-boyne-2026-10-30',
  'Contractor handed over for new R71 interchange at the ZCC headquarters in Boyne',
  'Traffic', '2026-10-30', 'Review Online', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/30/r450m-interchange-project-set-to-ease-congestion-at-moria/',
  'Raubex Construction has been named contractor for a R450 million interchange on the R71 at Boyne, with building expected to start in November 2026.',
  'Government has formally introduced Raubex Construction as the contractor for a new interchange on the R71 at Boyne, in the Polokwane municipal area. The bridge will serve the headquarters of the St Engenas Zion Christian Church, and the contractor was presented to the church''s leadership at a handover event.

According to the Limpopo government, the contract is worth R450 million. The provincial government is putting in R125 million through the Roads Agency Limpopo, with the national Department of Transport, SANRAL and the province working together on the project. The interchange will sit where the R71 meets the D4020 and will include flyover bridges, ramps, better drainage and traffic management facilities.

The R71 links Polokwane and Tzaneen and is one of the busiest roads in the province. Traffic is heaviest when very large numbers of worshippers travel to Moria for the church''s annual Easter gathering. The interchange is meant to separate local traffic from through traffic so that vehicles on the main road can keep moving, and to make access to the church grounds and nearby communities safer.

The Minister of Transport said work should run for about 18 months, starting in November 2026, subject to outstanding processes. Government says environmental approvals and questions over land parcels held by different parties still have to be settled. It adds that local businesses and communities are meant to take part in the work, and that labour will be recruited from surrounding communities.

Motorists should watch for construction notices on the R71 near Boyne once work begins.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/30/r450m-interchange-project-set-to-ease-congestion-at-moria/", "https://www.limpopo.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Government-hands-over-contractor-for-the-R450-Million-St-Engenas-ZCC-Interchange.pdf"]',
  'agent'
);
